Default wallpaper applied: `wallpaper-aurora`. Interesting that `stored: "aurora"` — applyWallpaper(save=true is the default) saved it. That's fine (init calls applyWallpaper(loadWallpaper()), and since the default is save=true, the default gets persisted on first load). Harmless — the default gets persisted. OK.

Next, test the context menu: dispatch a contextmenu event on an empty area of the desktop. Let me eval a synthetic contextmenu event at some coordinate, e.g., the center of the desktop, and check whether the menu opens.

Note: my handler is on desktopEl and checks e.target.closest('.window') / '.desktop-icon'. The empty area target would be #desktop or #windows. Dispatch:

```js
() => {
  const d = document.getElementById('desktop');
  const r = d.getBoundingClientRect();
  const ev = new MouseEvent('contextmenu', { bubbles: true, cancelable: true, clientX: r.left + r.width/2, clientY: r.top + r.height/2 });
  d.dispatchEvent(ev);
  const menu = document.getElementById('context-menu');
  return { open: menu.classList.contains('open'), left: menu.style.left, top: menu.style.top };
}
```

